{"term":"rot","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:562a1601c3d9d855e1","definition":"To suffer decomposition due to biological action, especially by fungi or bacteria.","example":"The apple left in the cupboard all that time had started to rot.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["putrefy","molder"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c743a41e2ff11b762d","definition":"To decline in function or utility.","example":"Your brain will rot if you spend so much time on the computer, Tony!","pos":"verb","synonyms":["putrefy","molder"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0b546bdd2d98802439","definition":"To (cause to) deteriorate in any way, as in morals; to corrupt.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["putrefy","molder"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8b3ff397c243076a9f","definition":"To make putrid; to cause to be wholly or partially decomposed by natural processes.","example":"to rot vegetable fiber","pos":"verb","synonyms":["putrefy","molder"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6a5a386731ba4f5dad","definition":"To spend a long period of time (in an unpleasant place or state).","example":"to rot in prison","pos":"verb","synonyms":["putrefy","molder"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0752acae1f272914f1","definition":"To expose, as flax, to a process of maceration, etc., for the purpose of separating the fiber; to ret.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["putrefy","molder"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2e1a7942c1ba636e75","definition":"To talk nonsense.","example":"“Did they hang you well?” said Porson.\n“Don’t rot,” said Mr Watkins; “I don’t like it.”","pos":"verb","synonyms":["putrefy","molder"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated, slang","register":"dated, slang","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:27b1ba6da51eef3a78","definition":"Damn; blast.","example":"\"Oh rot yer!\" exclaimed Fank, with a sudden flare of passion that at least carried with it the dignity of a genuine emotion; \"I've had just abart enough of you and your blinkin' game, Toady Joolby. Here, I'd sooner smash the bloody thing, straight, than be such a ruddy mug as to swallow any of your blahsted promises […]\"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["putrefy","molder"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"imperative, slang","register":"imperative, slang, transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktio